            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > This is solved by the third point in my simple impl details.\n> \n> I don't think it is. It sorts groups by priority ones, yes. But each 'statusline' evaluation might lead to different set of groups being displayed. The order in which they should be displayed might be different. As they were traversed in \"priority order\", there needs to be a way to convert them to \"display order\".\n\nSorry for the extra trouble but can you expand on this maybe?\n\nLet's say we have the following statusline\nA B                    C D\n\nSay I have groups D, C, B, A in descending order of priority. \n\nI would expect the lines to be:\nA B                    C D\nB                C D\n   C D\n    D",
