            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I see.\n\nOne trivial impl would be to assign an `__idx__` key or similar using an incremented counter variable to every group before sorting, creating a list of empty strings of num_groups length (both of these only done once), then assigning the string value of the group (empty if width + existing statusline width > `vim.api.nvim_win_get_width(0)` instead of previous `break`) at the `__idx__` position of the string list and returning concatenated list similar to `table.concat(parts, '')` in `mini.statusline`",
